# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository, and check it out as LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, line endings fall back to each developer's `core.autocrlf`: a Windows checkout
# gets a CRLF worktree, while clang-format, cmake-format, rustfmt and ruff all write LF. Every
# formatter run then rewrites whole files, and the `--check` gates in .githooks/pre-commit can
# never pass on Windows. `eol=lf` is the operative part — `text=auto` alone still yields CRLF
# worktrees there.
* text=auto eol=lf
